{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":14181009,"ns":0,"title":"PPP2R2A","revisions":[{"revid":1385770335,"parentid":1383233261,"minor":false,"timestamp":"2026-11-15T03:42:47Z","size":11794,"sha1":"da75cb18d061afef549508a4efb4b4dc1c461fac","slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","content":"{{cs1 config|name-list-style=vanc}}\n{{Short description|Enzyme found in humans}}\n{{Infobox_gene}}\n'''Serine/threonine-protein phosphatase 2A 55 kDa regulatory subunit B alpha isoform''' is an [[enzyme]] regulator that in humans is encoded by the ''PPP2R2A'' [[gene]].<ref name=\"pmid1849734\">{{cite journal | vauthors = Mayer RE, Hendrix P, Cron P, Matthies R, Stone SR, Goris J, Merlevede W, Hofsteenge J, Hemmings BA | title = Structure of the 55-kDa regulatory subunit of protein phosphatase 2A: evidence for a neuronal-specific isoform | journal = Biochemistry | volume = 30 | issue = 15 | pages = 3589–97 | date = Apr 1991 | pmid = 1849734 | doi = 10.1021/bi00229a001 }}</ref>\n\n== Function ==\n\nThe product of this gene belongs to the phosphatase 2 regulatory subunit B family. [[Protein phosphatase 2]] is one of the four major Ser/Thr phosphatases, and it is implicated in the negative control of cell growth and division. It consists of a common heteromeric core enzyme, which is composed of a catalytic subunit and a constant regulatory subunit, that associates with a variety of regulatory subunits. The B regulatory subunit might modulate substrate selectivity and catalytic activity. This gene encodes an alpha isoform of the regulatory subunit B55 subfamily.<ref name=\"entrez\">{{cite web | title = Entrez Gene: PPP2R2A protein phosphatase 2 (formerly 2A), regulatory subunit B, alpha isoform| url = https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/gene?Db=gene&Cmd=ShowDetailView&TermToSearch=5520}}</ref>\n\n== Interactions ==\n\nPPP2R2A has been shown to [[Protein-protein interaction|interact]] with:\n{{div col|colwidth=20em}}\n* [[P70-S6 Kinase 1]],<ref name = pmid10200280>{{cite journal | vauthors = Peterson RT, Desai BN, Hardwick JS, Schreiber SL | title = Protein phosphatase 2A interacts with the 70-kDa S6 kinase and is activated by inhibition of FKBP12-rapamycinassociated protein | journal = Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America | volume = 96 | issue = 8 | pages = 4438–42 | date = Apr 1999 | pmid = 10200280 | pmc = 16350 | doi =  10.1073/pnas.96.8.4438| bibcode = 1999PNAS...96.4438P | doi-access = free }}</ref><ref name = pmid16899564>{{cite journal | vauthors = Bishop JD, Nien WL, Dauphinee SM, Too CK | title = Prolactin activates mammalian target-of-rapamycin through phosphatidylinositol 3-kinase and stimulates phosphorylation of p70S6K and 4E-binding protein-1 in lymphoma cells | journal = The Journal of Endocrinology | volume = 190 | issue = 2 | pages = 307–12 | date = Aug 2006 | pmid = 16899564 | doi = 10.1677/joe.1.06368 | doi-access = free }}</ref> \n* [[PPP2CA]],<ref name = pmid1328247/><ref name = pmid18782753/>\n* [[PPP2R1A]],<ref name = pmid12370081/><ref name = pmid18782753>{{cite journal | vauthors = Goudreault M, D'Ambrosio LM, Kean MJ, Mullin MJ, Larsen BG, Sanchez A, Chaudhry S, Chen GI, Sicheri F, Nesvizhskii AI, Aebersold R, Raught B, Gingras AC | title = A PP2A phosphatase high density interaction network identifies a novel striatin-interacting phosphatase and kinase complex linked to the cerebral cavernous malformation 3 (CCM3) protein | journal = Molecular & Cellular Proteomics | volume = 8 | issue = 1 | pages = 157–71 | date = Jan 2009 | pmid = 18782753 | pmc = 2621004 | doi = 10.1074/mcp.M800266-MCP200 | doi-access = free }}</ref> \n* [[PPP2R1B]],<ref name = pmid1328247>{{cite journal | vauthors = Kamibayashi C, Lickteig RL, Estes R, Walter G, Mumby MC | title = Expression of the A subunit of protein phosphatase 2A and characterization of its interactions with the catalytic and regulatory subunits | journal = The Journal of Biological Chemistry | volu